1
00:00:09,984 --> 00:00:12,210
We are called the Fantastic Four.

2
00:00:12,235 --> 00:00:14,696
The former mic girl who wants
to become a news anchor.

3
00:00:14,697 --> 00:00:17,783
She ended up at a mall information
desk as a concierge.

4
00:00:17,784 --> 00:00:19,743
Good morning!
Welcome to Mega Lux mall!

5
00:00:19,744 --> 00:00:22,246
Enjoy your shopping!
Keep smiling!

6
00:00:22,247 --> 00:00:23,705
The taekwondo prodigy

7
00:00:23,706 --> 00:00:26,458
who wants to show off
his signature roundhouse kick.

8
00:00:26,459 --> 00:00:28,503
He is now kicking pests instead.

9
00:00:31,479 --> 00:00:33,980
The pink princess who wants
to become a housewife.

10
00:00:33,981 --> 00:00:37,734
She is now handling customers
as a customer service agent.

11
00:00:37,735 --> 00:00:39,861
Hello? This is Shop Shop Baby.

12
00:00:39,862 --> 00:00:43,365
The convenient store enthusiast
with a unique taste palate.

13
00:00:43,366 --> 00:00:46,701
He became a merchandise buyer
for a home shopping channel.

14
00:00:46,702 --> 00:00:49,246
Miss, is there a discount
if I order 2,000 packs?

15
00:00:49,247 --> 00:00:50,414
The Fantastic Four...

16
00:00:50,665 --> 00:00:52,917
Now, Fantastic No More.

17
00:00:53,417 --> 00:00:55,377
None of our dreams came true.

18
00:00:55,378 --> 00:00:57,880
But we continue to fight
through life's hardships.

19
00:00:58,381 --> 00:01:00,591
We are all fighting for our way.

20
00:01:11,853 --> 00:01:13,396
Why are you drunk again?

21
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:17,607
Aren’t you going to work again, darling?

22
00:01:17,608 --> 00:01:18,568
I’m going!

23
00:01:18,569 --> 00:01:21,653
No one will read the news
if I don’t show up.

24
00:01:21,654 --> 00:01:24,949
That’s not how you wear a tie properly.

25
00:01:29,537 --> 00:01:31,288
There, that looks better!

26
00:01:31,289 --> 00:01:35,250
Darling, the prices of goods are
getting even higher these days.

27
00:01:35,251 --> 00:01:36,377
What?

28
00:01:37,587 --> 00:01:40,213
The prices of goods keep rising,

29
00:01:40,214 --> 00:01:42,048
because of inflation.

30
00:01:42,049 --> 00:01:44,384
This has been made even
worse by the successive

31
00:01:44,385 --> 00:01:46,554
natural disasters hitting the country.

32
00:01:46,929 --> 00:01:49,348
Philippines, when will you ever recover?

33
00:01:52,727 --> 00:01:58,733
For Metro Filo News,
this is Aira Conti, reporting.

34
00:02:00,193 --> 00:02:04,237
Didn’t I tell you not to say
things I don’t understand?

35
00:02:04,238 --> 00:02:07,199
We’re not playing news reporting here.

36
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:10,369
But playing house is so boring.

37
00:02:13,289 --> 00:02:14,957
Oh, I’m just kidding!

38
00:02:15,333 --> 00:02:16,542
It’s really fun!

39
00:02:18,461 --> 00:02:20,837
I have to go to work now.

40
00:02:20,838 --> 00:02:23,674
Our children have to go to school.

41
00:02:24,258 --> 00:02:25,843
Son, it’s time to eat!

42
00:02:29,639 --> 00:02:30,681
Taekwondo!

43
00:02:33,935 --> 00:02:36,728
Hanz, you’re always
making Sally cry!

44
00:02:36,729 --> 00:02:39,815
Why do you always
have to break her toys?

45
00:02:40,191 --> 00:02:43,276
Mom, Aira’s hitting me again!

46
00:02:43,277 --> 00:02:46,447
Oh, sorry!
I’m sorry, sorry!

47
00:02:50,326 --> 00:02:51,785
Take out all your trash!

48
00:02:51,786 --> 00:02:55,039
Bring out all your trash!

49
00:02:55,331 --> 00:02:59,085
Separate biodegradable waste
from non-biodegradable waste!

50
00:03:00,206 --> 00:03:01,499
Hey! Sorry!

51
00:03:01,683 --> 00:03:02,975
Can you throw this as well?

52
00:03:02,976 --> 00:03:04,351
You always do this.

53
00:03:04,352 --> 00:03:06,604
- Oh, wow!
- Thanks.

54
00:03:07,991 --> 00:03:09,576
Take these too!

55
00:03:10,932 --> 00:03:12,058
Are you serious?

56
00:03:13,230 --> 00:03:14,750
Maybe you have some more,
don’t be shy.

57
00:03:15,190 --> 00:03:16,190
Wait!

58
00:03:16,316 --> 00:03:18,609
Thanks for taking our trash too, Hanz!

59
00:03:18,610 --> 00:03:19,610
You too?

60
00:03:20,612 --> 00:03:22,239
Wait, why do you have a luggage?

61
00:03:22,739 --> 00:03:23,657
Are you moving?

62
00:03:23,699 --> 00:03:26,341
No, Manny forgot his luggage again.

63
00:03:26,535 --> 00:03:27,735
Alright, I’ll get going, okay?

64
00:03:27,828 --> 00:03:28,828
See you later.

65
00:03:28,829 --> 00:03:29,829
Bye!

66
00:03:29,997 --> 00:03:31,290
Take care!

67
00:03:34,543 --> 00:03:35,543
Alright, then.

68
00:03:35,586 --> 00:03:37,296
Take the trash downstairs, babe.

69
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:39,841
“Babe”? What “babe”?

70
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,490
Why are you calling me “babe”?

71
00:03:42,005 --> 00:03:43,548
That sounds awful, Aira.

72
00:03:44,344 --> 00:03:45,344
Fine.

73
00:03:48,265 --> 00:03:49,807
Thank you, babe.

74
00:03:49,808 --> 00:03:52,436
I said don’t call me “babe”!
Come on!

75
00:03:54,346 --> 00:03:55,764
Such a brat.

76
00:04:00,569 --> 00:04:02,153
Here’s the latest scoop, girl!

77
00:04:02,154 --> 00:04:04,655
Joy is already two months pregnant!

78
00:04:04,656 --> 00:04:07,700
But it’s not that obvious yet.

79
00:04:07,943 --> 00:04:08,910
That’s what they said?

80
00:04:08,911 --> 00:04:10,954
Well, that’s what I heard.

81
00:04:11,688 --> 00:04:12,981
Right.

82
00:04:14,263 --> 00:04:15,849
- What about the person who saw it?
- Jess!

83
00:04:15,876 --> 00:04:16,918
What’s the latest gossip?

84
00:04:16,919 --> 00:04:18,252
Oh, Hanz!

85
00:04:18,253 --> 00:04:20,463
They say Joy is two months pregnant!

86
00:04:20,494 --> 00:04:21,494
Really?

87
00:04:52,788 --> 00:04:53,788
Hey, wait!

88
00:04:55,999 --> 00:04:57,417
Wow!

89
00:04:57,793 --> 00:04:58,877
All dressed up, huh?

90
00:04:59,461 --> 00:05:00,461
Where are you going?

91
00:05:00,963 --> 00:05:02,004
I have a hosting gig.

92
00:05:02,005 --> 00:05:04,174
A former college classmate recommended me.

93
00:05:04,633 --> 00:05:05,633
How do I look?

94
00:05:06,134 --> 00:05:08,303
- Uh...
- Do I look professional enough?

95
00:05:10,764 --> 00:05:11,698
You look like a human being now.

96
00:05:13,642 --> 00:05:15,477
Wait, look!

97
00:05:16,710 --> 00:05:18,253
Do I look pretty?

98
00:05:19,106 --> 00:05:20,815
Hmm...

99
00:05:20,816 --> 00:05:21,816
Don’t ask me things like that.

100
00:05:21,817 --> 00:05:23,277
I haven’t eaten yet, okay?

101
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:27,948
Wait, wait!

102
00:05:28,865 --> 00:05:31,410
Why can’t you admit that
you think I’m beautiful?

103
00:05:33,328 --> 00:05:34,538
Honestly...

104
00:05:36,373 --> 00:05:38,375
I’m really having a hard
time looking this pretty.

105
00:05:39,458 --> 00:05:42,169
It’s exhausting having
so many people fall for me.

106
00:05:49,136 --> 00:05:50,136
Hey, wait!

107
00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:53,181
Hey, hold on!

108
00:05:54,308 --> 00:05:55,726
Oh, good morning, Sir Jo.

109
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:58,603
Looks like that’s your
favorite bag now, huh?

110
00:05:58,854 --> 00:06:00,854
You use it almost every day.

111
00:06:01,023 --> 00:06:02,232
Well, it’s convenient to use.

112
00:06:02,774 --> 00:06:04,775
Don’t worry,
I’ll buy you another one.

113
00:06:04,776 --> 00:06:06,361
So you’ll have a spare.

114
00:06:06,778 --> 00:06:08,196
Aww.

115
00:06:08,982 --> 00:06:10,109
Really?

116
00:06:10,699 --> 00:06:13,492
You’re buying Baby Aira a new bag?

117
00:06:13,493 --> 00:06:15,078
You’ll do it for her?

118
00:06:22,044 --> 00:06:24,338
Baby Aira will have a new bag!

119
00:06:24,713 --> 00:06:26,506
You’re so annoying!

120
00:06:27,174 --> 00:06:29,050
Ouch!

121
00:06:29,051 --> 00:06:30,802
That hurts!

122
00:06:32,721 --> 00:06:35,432
Why would you hurt
a pretty girl like me?

123
00:06:44,858 --> 00:06:46,651
Where did you find these mango pastillas?

124
00:06:46,985 --> 00:06:49,404
Five shows have sold out
since we launched it.

125
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:52,115
Sir, people assume I just
have a strong appetite.

126
00:06:52,491 --> 00:06:53,992
But you know, I’m just a foodie.

127
00:06:54,743 --> 00:06:56,078
So when I first tasted it, Sir,

128
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:58,038
I knew it would be a hit.

129
00:06:58,205 --> 00:06:59,247
Nice, nice!

130
00:06:59,623 --> 00:07:02,417
We’ve sold 50,000 boxes
of mango pastillas already.

131
00:07:02,667 --> 00:07:03,752
Really, Sir?

132
00:07:04,628 --> 00:07:05,988
That means we’re making a fortune!

133
00:07:06,505 --> 00:07:08,130
Do I get a commission for that, Sir?

134
00:07:08,131 --> 00:07:10,674
Of course, you’ll get it!

135
00:07:10,675 --> 00:07:11,927
But just be patient, okay?

136
00:07:12,427 --> 00:07:15,679
You know you’re the most
valuable employee in this company.

137
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:16,680
Thank you, Sir.

138
00:07:16,848 --> 00:07:18,183
Welcome.
I’ll go ahead.

139
00:07:18,558 --> 00:07:19,643
Thank you, Sir.

140
00:07:20,477 --> 00:07:21,269
Congrats, Manny!

141
00:07:21,270 --> 00:07:23,854
- Congrats, Manny!
- Oh, thank you!

142
00:07:23,855 --> 00:07:25,399
- Congrats!
- Thank you.

143
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:27,359
Thank you.

144
00:07:27,359 --> 00:07:28,151
Congrats, Manny!

145
00:07:28,229 --> 00:07:29,229
Thank you.

146
00:07:53,927 --> 00:07:54,553
Sir Manny!

147
00:07:54,928 --> 00:07:55,928
Hey!

148
00:07:56,054 --> 00:07:57,346
- Marie.
- Did you happen to see the...

149
00:07:57,347 --> 00:07:59,266
gift I left on your desk?

150
00:08:00,914 --> 00:08:01,934
What gift?

151
00:08:01,969 --> 00:08:03,019
The chocolates.

152
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:05,397
I heard you have a sweet tooth.

153
00:08:06,565 --> 00:08:07,732
Oh, was that you from you?

154
00:08:09,276 --> 00:08:10,276
Thank you.

155
00:08:10,277 --> 00:08:11,945
- Marie, thank you.
- You’re welcome, Sir.

156
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:14,200
Just a little something
to relieve your stress.

157
00:08:14,656 --> 00:08:18,660
I noticed you seemed
to have a lot on your mind.

158
00:08:19,744 --> 00:08:21,344
A little sweetness to brighten your day.

159
00:08:22,873 --> 00:08:24,540
I’ve just got a lot
on my mind right now.

160
00:08:24,541 --> 00:08:26,918
Since TV shopping is about to launch.

161
00:08:27,294 --> 00:08:28,837
But Marie, I appreciate it.

162
00:08:28,962 --> 00:08:29,962
Thank you.

163
00:08:36,303 --> 00:08:37,553
I think she’s swooning.

164
00:08:37,554 --> 00:08:38,554
Yeah.

165
00:08:39,097 --> 00:08:41,137
So, how long have you been
working here, Sir Manny?

166
00:08:42,267 --> 00:08:43,642
Marie’s making a move, huh?

167
00:08:43,643 --> 00:08:46,312
Doesn’t she have a crush on Sir Manny?

168
00:08:46,313 --> 00:08:47,439
Yes, exactly!

169
00:08:48,064 --> 00:08:49,106
Girl power!

170
00:08:49,107 --> 00:08:50,233
That’s right.

171
00:08:52,944 --> 00:08:54,278
You should make the first move.

172
00:08:54,279 --> 00:08:55,572
You got that right.

173
00:09:03,663 --> 00:09:05,873
You’ve always been such a hard worker.

174
00:09:05,874 --> 00:09:08,001
That’s why I really admire you.

175
00:09:09,377 --> 00:09:11,295
Let me know when you’re free.

176
00:09:11,296 --> 00:09:12,797
I’ll treat you to coffee.

177
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:16,800
Huh?

178
00:09:17,636 --> 00:09:18,844
Are you listening, Sir?

179
00:09:18,845 --> 00:09:19,845
Oh...

180
00:09:20,055 --> 00:09:22,264
I said I’d treat you to
coffee when you’re free.

181
00:09:22,265 --> 00:09:23,642
Oh...

182
00:09:38,615 --> 00:09:40,408
I’ll go ahead.

183
00:09:48,750 --> 00:09:50,834
You left your luggage again.

184
00:09:50,835 --> 00:09:51,878
I’ll go there.

185
00:09:52,796 --> 00:09:54,630
I left the luggage in the hallway,

186
00:09:54,631 --> 00:09:56,466
in case someone might see us.

187
00:10:18,405 --> 00:10:20,323
Take that, too.

188
00:10:23,493 --> 00:10:26,496
I heard you broke another machine!

189
00:10:27,289 --> 00:10:29,207
Don't you know that's made in Germany?

190
00:10:29,958 --> 00:10:32,043
The parts are so expensive,
and now it’s broken.

191
00:10:32,419 --> 00:10:34,212
Oh, actually, Sir...

192
00:10:34,671 --> 00:10:35,671
It’s already fixed.

193
00:10:35,755 --> 00:10:36,381
It’s working now.

194
00:10:36,382 --> 00:10:37,465
It was just clogged.

195
00:10:38,758 --> 00:10:41,011
I told you to clean it regularly.

196
00:10:41,511 --> 00:10:42,804
That’s not even my machine.

197
00:10:43,221 --> 00:10:44,221
Huh?

198
00:10:44,514 --> 00:10:45,765
Were you drunk last night?

199
00:10:46,016 --> 00:10:47,017
Then whose is it?

200
00:10:48,435 --> 00:10:49,644
-That’s yours —
-Just leave it!

201
00:10:49,894 --> 00:10:51,521
Just be careful next time!

202
00:10:52,355 --> 00:10:53,064
Alright, then.

203
00:10:53,356 --> 00:10:54,356
Put it back inside.

204
00:10:55,525 --> 00:10:56,525
Alright, boss.

205
00:10:59,654 --> 00:11:00,739
Sir, that’s your machine.

206
00:11:02,282 --> 00:11:04,002
It's done.
Why are you still bringing it up?

207
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:06,536
You’re lucky you weren’t fired.

208
00:11:08,496 --> 00:11:09,331
Go, put it inside.

209
00:11:09,332 --> 00:11:10,874
I’m going to get some coffee.

210
00:11:25,347 --> 00:11:26,347
Hey, Phil?

211
00:11:26,556 --> 00:11:28,683
Hanz, are you busy?

212
00:11:29,267 --> 00:11:30,434
I’m not doing anything.

213
00:11:30,435 --> 00:11:31,810
Can you be a stand-in
for my game show?

214
00:11:31,811 --> 00:11:32,811
A stand-in?

215
00:11:34,481 --> 00:11:36,523
Why, can I just join in like that?

216
00:11:36,524 --> 00:11:38,108
I’ll take care of it. Just be there.

217
00:11:38,109 --> 00:11:39,110
All right, I’m in!

218
00:11:42,405 --> 00:11:43,632
Flowers.

219
00:11:43,657 --> 00:11:44,924
Is the food all set?

220
00:11:44,949 --> 00:11:46,116
Yes, it’s on the way.

221
00:11:46,117 --> 00:11:47,534
Cameraman, photographer?

222
00:11:47,535 --> 00:11:49,496
Have all our guests confirmed?

223
00:11:50,455 --> 00:11:51,122
Uhm...

224
00:11:51,348 --> 00:11:52,199
Excuse me?

225
00:11:52,290 --> 00:11:53,683
Okay, go ahead and check.

226
00:11:53,708 --> 00:11:55,292
- Oh, Aira right?
- Yes.

227
00:11:55,293 --> 00:11:57,252
I got your text saying you were here.

228
00:11:57,253 --> 00:11:58,462
- Melody here.
- Oh, hello!

229
00:11:58,463 --> 00:12:00,381
Guada recommended you to me.

230
00:12:00,382 --> 00:12:02,050
She said you used to host?

231
00:12:02,342 --> 00:12:03,384
Yes.

232
00:12:03,385 --> 00:12:06,387
But it’s been quite a while
since I last held a mic.

233
00:12:06,388 --> 00:12:07,388
But I can do it.

234
00:12:07,389 --> 00:12:08,056
Okay.

235
00:12:08,057 --> 00:12:10,724
No worries.
This is just a small party.

236
00:12:10,725 --> 00:12:14,562
Birthday celebration with some
corporate people and partners.

237
00:12:14,813 --> 00:12:16,689
Less than 20 people or so.

238
00:12:16,690 --> 00:12:19,067
The celebrant just requested a host.

239
00:12:19,401 --> 00:12:22,778
But they told us the program
should flow spontaneously.

240
00:12:22,779 --> 00:12:23,779
- Can you do that?
- Yes.

241
00:12:23,780 --> 00:12:24,822
I’ll take care of it.

242
00:12:24,823 --> 00:12:25,823
Okay.

243
00:12:26,062 --> 00:12:28,534
But you’re actually very early.

244
00:12:28,535 --> 00:12:30,035
The party is at 5 p.m.

245
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:31,570
It’s only 12 p.m.

246
00:12:31,871 --> 00:12:32,996
Oh, no!

247
00:12:32,997 --> 00:12:35,310
I just really need
to check out the venue.

248
00:12:35,335 --> 00:12:36,500
Just to familiarize myself with it.

249
00:12:36,641 --> 00:12:37,641
I see.

250
00:12:39,337 --> 00:12:41,880
Anyway, maybe I’ll have lunch first.

251
00:12:41,881 --> 00:12:42,757
I’ll come back later.

252
00:12:42,758 --> 00:12:44,133
Okay, sure. See you!

253
00:12:44,134 --> 00:12:45,413
- Thank you!
- Bye.

254
00:12:47,654 --> 00:12:49,155
How excited are you, Aira?

255
00:12:49,821 --> 00:12:50,947
This is embarrassing.

256
00:12:53,859 --> 00:12:56,612
Philippines! Are you game?

257
00:12:57,021 --> 00:12:58,689
Game!

258
00:12:58,690 --> 00:13:02,235
It’s Quiz Time!

259
00:13:05,655 --> 00:13:07,824
For our first question,

260
00:13:08,663 --> 00:13:12,832
What does the old Tagalog word.

261
00:13:13,357 --> 00:13:14,692
“ALIMPUYO” mean?

262
00:13:15,377 --> 00:13:19,214
A. A gust of wind that
swirls in a circular motion.

263
00:13:20,030 --> 00:13:23,242
B. Bad temper or intense anger.

264
00:13:24,174 --> 00:13:27,927
Or C. A sudden downpour
in the middle of the day.

265
00:13:28,261 --> 00:13:29,763
And, go!

266
00:13:31,181 --> 00:13:32,264
Yes, Player Number 4.

267
00:13:32,265 --> 00:13:33,265
What’s your answer?

268
00:13:33,933 --> 00:13:34,933
Uh...

269
00:13:36,895 --> 00:13:37,895
I think it’s B!

270
00:13:38,855 --> 00:13:40,064
It sounds like an insult.

271
00:13:40,565 --> 00:13:43,849
You know, when you’re really angry,
you just say...

272
00:13:44,569 --> 00:13:45,569
“You’re Alimpuyo!”

273
00:13:47,363 --> 00:13:48,698
Yes, correct. Sounds right.

274
00:13:49,741 --> 00:13:51,201
What is this person talking about?

275
00:13:52,179 --> 00:13:53,305
Phil, was he screened?

276
00:13:54,662 --> 00:13:55,388
Sorry, sir.

277
00:13:55,413 --> 00:13:57,165
He’s just a stand-in.

278
00:13:57,707 --> 00:13:59,107
The actual player couldn’t make it.

279
00:14:00,877 --> 00:14:01,795
Uh...

280
00:14:01,796 --> 00:14:04,421
B is wrong.

281
00:14:04,422 --> 00:14:06,883
Sorry Player Number 4, you’re out!

282
00:14:08,843 --> 00:14:09,927
Anybody for a steal?

283
00:14:09,928 --> 00:14:11,554
And, go!

284
00:14:12,806 --> 00:14:13,932
Yes, Player Number 8?

285
00:14:14,390 --> 00:14:16,266
If you answer this question correctly,

286
00:14:16,267 --> 00:14:18,310
you have a chance to
advance to the next round.

287
00:14:18,428 --> 00:14:19,638
What’s your answer?

288
00:14:20,146 --> 00:14:21,439
The answer is letter A.

289
00:14:22,148 --> 00:14:24,234
A gust of wind that
swirls in a circular motion.

290
00:14:24,818 --> 00:14:26,236
Whirlwind in English.

291
00:14:26,778 --> 00:14:28,821
A is correct!

292
00:14:28,822 --> 00:14:30,823
Congratulations, Player Number 8!

293
00:14:30,824 --> 00:14:32,325
You advance to the next round.

294
00:14:33,785 --> 00:14:35,537
And for our next question.

295
00:14:44,003 --> 00:14:45,003
That’s all?

296
00:14:45,255 --> 00:14:47,841
It's only good for one person, sir.

297
00:15:02,355 --> 00:15:03,689
Sir, that’s quite a lot.

298
00:15:03,690 --> 00:15:04,690
Huh?

299
00:15:04,858 --> 00:15:05,984
The serving is so small.

300
00:15:06,317 --> 00:15:07,235
Is there any more food?

301
00:15:07,318 --> 00:15:08,318
Here, sir.

302
00:15:08,778 --> 00:15:09,404
Chicken?

303
00:15:09,571 --> 00:15:11,154
Stir-fried green beans, sir.

304
00:15:11,155 --> 00:15:12,031
No, I don’t want that.

305
00:15:12,032 --> 00:15:13,032
I don’t eat vegetables.

306
00:15:13,741 --> 00:15:14,993
Spring rolls, sir?

307
00:15:15,535 --> 00:15:16,786
Yes, lumpia.

308
00:15:19,497 --> 00:15:20,498
How about this, sir?

309
00:15:20,832 --> 00:15:22,083
This will do.

310
00:15:30,675 --> 00:15:31,675
Hey!

311
00:15:31,843 --> 00:15:33,427
You’re my former classmate, aren’t you?

312
00:15:33,428 --> 00:15:34,428
The smart one.

313
00:15:35,169 --> 00:15:36,169
Right?

314
00:15:36,556 --> 00:15:39,100
I knew you looked familiar.

315
00:15:41,359 --> 00:15:42,527
I don’t remember.

316
00:15:46,024 --> 00:15:48,109
I’m Hanz.

317
00:15:48,543 --> 00:15:49,543
Hanz Araneta.

318
00:15:50,947 --> 00:15:52,323
What was your name again?

319
00:15:53,948 --> 00:15:54,948
Marvin.

320
00:15:55,607 --> 00:15:57,109
Sorry, I really don’t remember.

321
00:15:57,493 --> 00:15:58,328
Marvin.

322
00:15:58,329 --> 00:16:00,983
Well, it has been quite a while.

323
00:16:01,789 --> 00:16:04,083
So how have you been?

324
00:16:06,387 --> 00:16:07,387
Wait.

325
00:16:08,796 --> 00:16:09,923
Don’t you want this anymore?

326
00:16:11,329 --> 00:16:12,330
Can I have it?

327
00:16:16,262 --> 00:16:17,555
Nice!

328
00:16:20,516 --> 00:16:21,516
Marvin?

329
00:16:22,310 --> 00:16:23,310
Phil.

330
00:16:23,519 --> 00:16:25,146
Producer of Quiz Time.

331
00:16:25,521 --> 00:16:26,606
Can I talk to you?

332
00:16:28,566 --> 00:16:29,942
I swear, you're something else.

333
00:16:29,943 --> 00:16:31,152
You’re so smart.

334
00:16:32,028 --> 00:16:33,029
Thank you.

335
00:16:33,363 --> 00:16:34,603
I’ll get straight to the point.

336
00:16:35,114 --> 00:16:37,991
We’re having a year-end party
with the past winners.

337
00:16:37,992 --> 00:16:39,201
So we were hoping you could join us...

338
00:16:39,202 --> 00:16:40,703
Wait, classmate,

339
00:16:41,454 --> 00:16:42,454
do you remember me now?

340
00:16:44,916 --> 00:16:47,285
I was the one who borrowed
your shirt before.

341
00:16:47,418 --> 00:16:49,921
You even watched my taekwondo match.

342
00:16:50,296 --> 00:16:51,047
And I won that match.

343
00:16:51,048 --> 00:16:52,673
I was doing this.

344
00:16:52,674 --> 00:16:54,234
I showed off your shirt just like this.

345
00:16:55,969 --> 00:16:57,691
Do you remember now?

346
00:16:59,305 --> 00:16:59,973
No.

347
00:17:00,223 --> 00:17:01,223
Not really.

348
00:17:02,141 --> 00:17:03,142
- Hanz!
- What?

349
00:17:03,393 --> 00:17:04,933
Stop bothering Marvin.

350
00:17:07,522 --> 00:17:08,522
Uhm..

351
00:17:09,607 --> 00:17:11,566
I’m sorry, I have to answer this.

352
00:17:11,567 --> 00:17:12,860
Yeah, take your time.

353
00:17:17,490 --> 00:17:18,533
Look,

354
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:19,993
what if he doesn’t come back?

355
00:17:22,111 --> 00:17:23,111
Anyway.

356
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:26,498
We have gift certificates to give away.

357
00:17:26,499 --> 00:17:29,168
But yours is under the
original player’s name.

358
00:17:31,504 --> 00:17:32,504
I’m sorry.

359
00:17:33,089 --> 00:17:34,090
That’s okay.

360
00:17:36,342 --> 00:17:37,969
Do you actually know that doctor?

361
00:17:39,429 --> 00:17:40,429
Hold on.

362
00:17:40,805 --> 00:17:41,805
He’s a doctor now?

363
00:17:42,223 --> 00:17:43,223
Is it true?

364
00:17:43,766 --> 00:17:45,476
Maybe you could...

365
00:17:46,728 --> 00:17:48,479
convince him to come
to the year-end party.

366
00:17:49,230 --> 00:17:50,064
Come on.

367
00:17:50,231 --> 00:17:51,774
As you can see,
he’s just ignoring me.

368
00:17:52,108 --> 00:17:53,609
I just saw him again today.

369
00:17:55,355 --> 00:17:56,355
Wait a second.

370
00:17:58,656 --> 00:18:00,323
Here he goes again.

371
00:18:00,324 --> 00:18:01,404
Miss, can I have some more?

372
00:18:02,535 --> 00:18:03,535
Uh...

373
00:18:04,203 --> 00:18:05,203
Is that so?

374
00:18:06,205 --> 00:18:07,205
Okay.

375
00:18:08,124 --> 00:18:09,124
Oh!

376
00:18:09,167 --> 00:18:10,167
Wait.

377
00:18:12,295 --> 00:18:14,175
This is for you,
because you came to my rescue.

378
00:18:15,214 --> 00:18:16,214
No, it’s okay.

379
00:18:16,799 --> 00:18:18,009
We’re friends, after all.

380
00:18:18,593 --> 00:18:19,427
Come on.

381
00:18:19,428 --> 00:18:21,471
I asked you to come here,
so just accept it.

382
00:18:23,931 --> 00:18:24,931
Oh, wait.

383
00:18:25,141 --> 00:18:26,285
I have another show to go to.

384
00:18:26,309 --> 00:18:27,736
Uhm, I’ll go there first.

385
00:18:27,761 --> 00:18:28,679
Just message me, okay?

386
00:18:28,704 --> 00:18:29,704
Sure.

387
00:18:30,813 --> 00:18:31,813
Thanks, Hanz!

388
00:18:45,661 --> 00:18:46,741
Do you have any more, Miss?

389
00:18:54,962 --> 00:18:56,338
Miss Julia!

390
00:18:56,339 --> 00:18:58,965
- Can we take a picture with you?
- Sure, of course.

391
00:18:58,966 --> 00:18:59,966
Let’s take a picture.

392
00:19:01,177 --> 00:19:02,220
One more, please.

393
00:19:03,137 --> 00:19:05,241
- Could we get a video greeting too?
- Okay, sure.

394
00:19:05,266 --> 00:19:07,018
- For Abby.
- Abby, okay.

395
00:19:07,517 --> 00:19:09,309
Hi, Abby!
Hope you enjoy your day.

396
00:19:09,310 --> 00:19:10,144
God bless.

397
00:19:10,145 --> 00:19:13,314
- Thank you!
- Thank you.

398
00:19:47,348 --> 00:19:49,392
I don’t know why I’m so nervous.

399
00:19:58,901 --> 00:20:00,193
I feel like a teenager

400
00:20:00,194 --> 00:20:04,031
that’s about to meet her
first love after so many years.

401
00:20:07,201 --> 00:20:09,245
It’s an overwhelming feeling.

402
00:20:10,371 --> 00:20:13,249
But the excitement and
happiness are stronger.

403
00:20:14,379 --> 00:20:15,422
Because...

404
00:20:34,770 --> 00:20:36,397
when I’m holding the mic,

405
00:20:37,398 --> 00:20:39,150
I own the beat.

406
00:20:39,530 --> 00:20:41,073
The whole world is mine.

407
00:20:42,236 --> 00:20:43,278
Good evening, everyone.

408
00:20:43,279 --> 00:20:45,364
May I have your attention, please?

409
00:20:49,535 --> 00:20:51,953
There, now that I have your attention.

410
00:20:52,136 --> 00:20:53,580
My name is Aira Conti.

411
00:20:53,581 --> 00:20:55,790
A concierge at Mega Lux Mall by day,

412
00:20:55,791 --> 00:20:57,960
and your private host for tonight.

413
00:21:01,418 --> 00:21:05,401
Before we start, I’d like to greet our
celebrant a happy birthday.

414
00:21:05,426 --> 00:21:06,968
[In Chinese] Happy Birthday to you.

415
00:21:06,969 --> 00:21:08,553
- Am I right?
- Sorry, I’m late.

416
00:21:08,554 --> 00:21:09,138
Not at all.

417
00:21:09,139 --> 00:21:10,680
- It just started.
- Thank you very much.

418
00:21:10,681 --> 00:21:12,557
Because of your birthday,

419
00:21:12,558 --> 00:21:14,268
you’ve given me a gig.

420
00:21:15,937 --> 00:21:17,437
I may not know you personally,

421
00:21:17,438 --> 00:21:20,233
but I know in my heart that
you are a good person.

422
00:21:20,566 --> 00:21:21,942
Kind and handsome, too.

423
00:21:21,943 --> 00:21:22,485
Am I right?

424
00:21:22,486 --> 00:21:23,486
Do you guys agree?

425
00:21:23,720 --> 00:21:25,000
She has such a warm personality.

426
00:21:25,630 --> 00:21:26,631
Where did you find her?

427
00:21:27,531 --> 00:21:28,424
I don’t know.

428
00:21:28,449 --> 00:21:29,325
I’m just a guest.

429
00:21:29,326 --> 00:21:32,096
So, everyone here is very
lucky to have you.

430
00:21:32,121 --> 00:21:35,538
As their boss, their business partner,
and as their friend.

431
00:21:35,793 --> 00:21:41,871
Now, let’s kick off this celebration with
a birthday song for our celebrant, Mr. Lee!

432
00:21:42,338 --> 00:21:50,338
[In Chinese] Happy Birthday to you.

433
00:22:07,280 --> 00:22:08,572
Happy birthday, Mom.

434
00:22:08,698 --> 00:22:09,781
Thank you, dear.

435
00:22:09,782 --> 00:22:10,782
Let’s turn it on.

436
00:22:10,950 --> 00:22:12,618
Why did you buy this?

437
00:22:12,910 --> 00:22:13,536
Hey!

438
00:22:13,703 --> 00:22:16,080
You should’ve saved
that money for yourself.

439
00:22:17,575 --> 00:22:19,202
But — Oh!

440
00:22:19,875 --> 00:22:21,501
It’s effective!

441
00:22:21,502 --> 00:22:23,879
I can feel it right away in my hand.

442
00:22:25,298 --> 00:22:27,733
- Here, there’s another one.
- It feels so good.

443
00:22:27,758 --> 00:22:29,384
Just use it like this on
the parts that hurt.

444
00:22:29,385 --> 00:22:31,345
- Try it.
- Here, here.

445
00:22:34,015 --> 00:22:35,055
- Try it.
- Ouch, that hurts!

446
00:22:35,190 --> 00:22:36,108
Oh, dear.

447
00:22:36,309 --> 00:22:37,601
Wait a second.

448
00:22:37,810 --> 00:22:39,687
There! Oh, wow!

449
00:22:41,605 --> 00:22:42,857
Oh, that feels good.

450
00:22:43,161 --> 00:22:44,281
This is expensive, isn’t it?

451
00:22:44,525 --> 00:22:46,211
- Not really.
- It is expensive.

452
00:22:46,236 --> 00:22:47,362
But it does feel good.

453
00:22:48,237 --> 00:22:49,822
- Thank you.
- You’re so noisy!

454
00:22:50,209 --> 00:22:51,209
Can you keep it down?

455
00:22:51,234 --> 00:22:52,527
We’re eating!

456
00:22:56,996 --> 00:22:58,789
Can you stop yelling at Mom?

457
00:23:00,041 --> 00:23:01,500
It’s her birthday today.

458
00:23:04,712 --> 00:23:06,101
Where did that come from?

459
00:23:07,490 --> 00:23:09,326
It's probably not stolen, right?

460
00:23:10,760 --> 00:23:12,859
He’s starting over.

461
00:23:13,804 --> 00:23:15,265
Stop scolding him.

462
00:23:16,349 --> 00:23:18,059
He might won’t visit
again because of you.

463
00:23:18,434 --> 00:23:19,769
Just let him be.

464
00:23:20,320 --> 00:23:21,905
Don’t mind him, dear.

465
00:23:26,525 --> 00:23:28,194
I didn’t steal anything.
I have a job.

466
00:23:28,986 --> 00:23:29,986
You know...

467
00:23:31,280 --> 00:23:34,758
Maybe you should’ve just
become a taekwondo instructor.

468
00:23:35,493 --> 00:23:36,743
That’s your field.

469
00:23:36,899 --> 00:23:38,609
That’s what you’re good at.

470
00:23:40,291 --> 00:23:43,002
Do you know that if
you search my name online,

471
00:23:43,904 --> 00:23:47,203
the only thing that comes up is
what happened on November 3, 2017?

472
00:23:47,963 --> 00:23:48,923
Now, Dad, tell me.

473
00:23:48,924 --> 00:23:50,404
Would anyone even enroll in my class?

474
00:23:51,717 --> 00:23:53,094
Don't be such a coward.

475
00:23:53,932 --> 00:23:54,932
Hmm?

476
00:23:55,346 --> 00:23:57,556
Why can’t you just move on?

477
00:23:59,725 --> 00:24:01,461
How are you supposed
to succeed in life like that?

478
00:24:02,269 --> 00:24:03,270
That’s right!

479
00:24:05,815 --> 00:24:06,941
I’m worthless, aren’t I?

480
00:24:07,608 --> 00:24:09,265
Taekwondo is the only thing I know.

481
00:24:11,491 --> 00:24:13,929
I can’t succeed at anything else.

482
00:24:15,658 --> 00:24:16,951
But, Dad, you know what?

483
00:24:18,786 --> 00:24:20,506
If you’ll force me to become an instructor,

484
00:24:21,622 --> 00:24:22,789
I won’t do it.

485
00:24:26,460 --> 00:24:27,460
Fine, then.

486
00:24:28,212 --> 00:24:29,964
It’s done.
Why are you still angry?

487
00:24:31,882 --> 00:24:33,300
It’s not that I’m angry.

488
00:24:35,928 --> 00:24:39,348
I’m afraid that if I try once more,
I’ll end up loving it again.

489
00:24:40,391 --> 00:24:41,951
I’m not even thinking about it anymore.

490
00:24:42,393 --> 00:24:44,520
I don't want to end up disappointed again.

491
00:24:46,605 --> 00:24:48,482
If only you had acted like a father,

492
00:24:50,234 --> 00:24:52,194
maybe I wouldn’t have
turned out so useless.

493
00:24:53,362 --> 00:24:54,988
Maybe I wouldn’t have
had to throw the match!

494
00:24:54,989 --> 00:24:55,906
You bastard...

495
00:24:55,907 --> 00:24:58,950
S-stop it.
Rachel will hear you.

496
00:24:58,951 --> 00:25:00,744
Oh, and about Rachel, too.

497
00:25:00,864 --> 00:25:03,033
Aren’t you supposed to be
the one taking care of her?

498
00:25:03,919 --> 00:25:04,961
Why me?

499
00:25:05,708 --> 00:25:07,375
Why does it always have to be me?

500
00:25:07,376 --> 00:25:08,502
Why is it always me?

501
00:25:13,841 --> 00:25:14,841
I’m sorry, Mom.

502
00:25:30,483 --> 00:25:31,483
Boom!

503
00:25:32,693 --> 00:25:33,693
Wow!

504
00:25:34,570 --> 00:25:35,988
That was a great kick.

505
00:25:36,321 --> 00:25:37,614
His hook was weak, though.

506
00:25:38,942 --> 00:25:41,062
You don't give out compliments
easily, do you, Coach?

507
00:25:41,087 --> 00:25:42,287
You never approve of anything.

508
00:25:43,889 --> 00:25:45,015
What are you talking about?

509
00:25:46,141 --> 00:25:48,977
He's pretty generous
when it comes to his first love.

510
00:25:51,503 --> 00:25:53,630
Coach, is he really that good?

511
00:25:54,032 --> 00:25:55,159
Is he better than me?

512
00:25:56,869 --> 00:25:59,413
You think too highly of yourself.

513
00:25:59,939 --> 00:26:03,609
And he always thinks too little of himself.

514
00:26:42,372 --> 00:26:43,372
Hi, Coach.

515
00:26:49,994 --> 00:26:50,994
What a surprise.

516
00:26:51,737 --> 00:26:54,239
I’ve been here for so long,
and you’re only visiting now.

517
00:26:56,063 --> 00:26:59,782
Mom packed me so much food.

518
00:27:00,554 --> 00:27:02,807
I thought I’d share some with you, Coach.

519
00:27:10,492 --> 00:27:11,996
Call your father.

520
00:27:12,371 --> 00:27:15,374
He won’t be able to sleep
because you just left like that.

521
00:27:15,583 --> 00:27:17,626
Rachel’s asking about you too.

522
00:27:21,429 --> 00:27:22,430
Bro!

523
00:27:23,366 --> 00:27:25,961
I heard your kicks are legendary.

524
00:27:28,637 --> 00:27:29,637
So?

525
00:27:30,681 --> 00:27:31,849
Let’s have a match.

526
00:27:36,312 --> 00:27:38,897
I want to learn your moves.

527
00:27:39,982 --> 00:27:41,400
And I’m curious to see them.

528
00:27:42,067 --> 00:27:43,527
You’re Coach’s favorite, after all.

529
00:27:44,653 --> 00:27:47,211
I’m just a little jealous.

530
00:27:47,948 --> 00:27:49,033
Are you drunk?

531
00:27:52,077 --> 00:27:53,871
Oh, right.

532
00:27:54,494 --> 00:27:56,621
You don’t fight anymore, do you?

533
00:27:59,418 --> 00:28:00,418
How about this?

534
00:28:01,503 --> 00:28:03,172
Let’s bet ₱3,000.

535
00:28:04,006 --> 00:28:05,007
Light match.

536
00:28:05,674 --> 00:28:07,359
Just a light match, I promise.

537
00:28:07,384 --> 00:28:08,552
Go to sleep already.

538
00:28:09,011 --> 00:28:10,012
You’re drunk.

539
00:28:12,681 --> 00:28:13,681
All right, fine.

540
00:28:14,141 --> 00:28:15,183
Forget about it.

541
00:28:15,355 --> 00:28:17,565
You don’t seem proud of being a fighter.

542
00:28:18,646 --> 00:28:19,646
Besides...

543
00:28:19,938 --> 00:28:25,469
I guess it would be unfair for
someone like you to fight a pro like me.

544
00:28:35,579 --> 00:28:36,579
Fight.

545
00:28:43,045 --> 00:28:44,045
Come on, let’s spar.

546
00:29:01,897 --> 00:29:02,897
Here, Hanz.

547
00:29:03,174 --> 00:29:04,591
You haven’t used this in a while.

548
00:29:04,616 --> 00:29:05,701
I hope it still fits.

549
00:29:05,919 --> 00:29:07,044
No need, Coach.

550
00:29:07,069 --> 00:29:08,279
I’m not going to use that.

551
00:29:09,751 --> 00:29:11,835
Wait, are you sure you won’t wear it?

552
00:29:11,860 --> 00:29:13,060
You won’t have any protection?

553
00:29:13,276 --> 00:29:15,319
Do you think you can beat me?

554
00:29:16,286 --> 00:29:17,412
You’re right.

555
00:29:17,413 --> 00:29:19,122
You’re no amateur.

556
00:29:19,123 --> 00:29:21,083
Just think of this as a warm-up, okay?

557
00:29:22,084 --> 00:29:23,252
Remove this.

558
00:29:29,323 --> 00:29:30,489
This will be your first and last round.

559
00:29:30,514 --> 00:29:32,433
Let’s see how good you are.

560
00:29:35,639 --> 00:29:36,682
Go.

561
00:29:39,768 --> 00:29:41,019
Hello!

562
00:29:42,062 --> 00:29:43,062
Come on!

563
00:29:46,525 --> 00:29:47,818
Coach, what is this?!

564
00:29:48,173 --> 00:29:49,716
Coach, I haven’t even warmed up yet!

565
00:29:51,363 --> 00:29:52,489
Get up, Hanz!

566
00:29:59,997 --> 00:30:00,997
Go!

567
00:30:06,086 --> 00:30:07,086
Let’s go!

568
00:30:09,757 --> 00:30:11,257
More kicks, more kicks.

569
00:30:11,258 --> 00:30:12,301
Keep kicking!

570
00:30:34,490 --> 00:30:35,949
That’s enough!

571
00:30:36,617 --> 00:30:37,781
Stop it!

572
00:30:38,225 --> 00:30:39,585
I still have a food truck to open!

573
00:30:40,696 --> 00:30:42,615
Looks like he’s useless!

574
00:31:13,153 --> 00:31:14,153
Coach.

575
00:31:15,614 --> 00:31:17,334
Are you going to set up
in our place again?

576
00:31:17,616 --> 00:31:19,136
I’m not going to set up there anymore.

577
00:31:20,035 --> 00:31:21,285
See, Coach?

578
00:31:21,286 --> 00:31:22,286
You saw it.

579
00:31:23,080 --> 00:31:24,414
I can’t fight anymore.

580
00:31:25,165 --> 00:31:26,416
I’m hopeless.

581
00:31:27,086 --> 00:31:28,627
I’m back to square one.

582
00:31:30,921 --> 00:31:32,464
But you know, Coach...

583
00:31:33,421 --> 00:31:34,922
It actually feels good...

584
00:31:35,634 --> 00:31:38,846
to get beaten up again.

585
00:31:42,307 --> 00:31:43,559
Are you serious?

586
00:31:44,351 --> 00:31:45,560
Get out of here!

587
00:31:45,561 --> 00:31:47,061
Don’t disturb me!

588
00:31:47,062 --> 00:31:48,062
Leave!

589
00:31:48,564 --> 00:31:50,065
I still have to make a living!

590
00:32:07,499 --> 00:32:08,542
Where is it?

591
00:32:09,626 --> 00:32:11,253
I know I just tucked it in here.

592
00:32:14,381 --> 00:32:15,381
Huh?

593
00:32:19,845 --> 00:32:21,305
It’s really not here.

594
00:32:33,191 --> 00:32:34,651
- Hello?
- Hello, Hanz?

595
00:32:35,063 --> 00:32:36,439
What’s your problem?

596
00:32:37,607 --> 00:32:38,984
Can you pick me up?

597
00:32:39,114 --> 00:32:40,114
My wallet’s missing.

598
00:32:40,115 --> 00:32:41,617
I’ve been looking for it.

599
00:32:42,732 --> 00:32:44,294
You’re so careless!

600
00:32:44,995 --> 00:32:46,513
And I’m not your driver, okay?

601
00:32:46,997 --> 00:32:48,457
I don’t even have my own car.

602
00:32:49,429 --> 00:32:52,140
Oh, it’s mic girl again.

603
00:32:52,878 --> 00:32:53,878
Okay, fine.

604
00:32:54,087 --> 00:32:55,714
Never mind. I’ll just walk.

605
00:32:55,923 --> 00:32:56,923
Oh, don’t!

606
00:32:57,299 --> 00:32:58,592
Fine, where are you?

607
00:32:59,801 --> 00:33:01,093
I’ll send you the address, okay?

608
00:33:01,094 --> 00:33:02,511
Please, come get me.

609
00:33:02,512 --> 00:33:05,457
And could you bring
the slippers you gave me?

610
00:33:05,482 --> 00:33:06,783
I just left it outside to dry.

611
00:33:06,972 --> 00:33:08,557
Okay? Thank you.

612
00:33:09,186 --> 00:33:10,145
You sure have a lot of demands.

613
00:33:10,146 --> 00:33:11,529
I’m not your servant.

614
00:33:11,813 --> 00:33:13,482
Huh? H-hello?

615
00:33:14,858 --> 00:33:16,068
The nerve to hung up on me.

616
00:33:17,152 --> 00:33:18,152
Coach!

617
00:33:18,236 --> 00:33:19,422
I can’t come with you anymore.

618
00:33:19,595 --> 00:33:20,595
Huh?

619
00:33:26,078 --> 00:33:28,829
Aira, the client loved you.

620
00:33:28,830 --> 00:33:30,081
Really?

621
00:33:30,082 --> 00:33:32,041
That’s a relief.

622
00:33:32,183 --> 00:33:33,767
They were really impressed with you.

623
00:33:33,792 --> 00:33:35,252
Hosting comes so naturally to you.

624
00:33:35,253 --> 00:33:37,667
Why don’t you make it a full-time job?

625
00:33:38,507 --> 00:33:40,092
I wish it were that easy.

626
00:33:40,634 --> 00:33:44,553
Anyway, I’ll deposit your
payment tomorrow, okay?

627
00:33:44,554 --> 00:33:47,598
Sorry, I forgot to have the cheque signed.

628
00:33:47,739 --> 00:33:49,073
That’s fine.

629
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:50,620
It’s okay. Thank you so much.

630
00:33:50,978 --> 00:33:52,228
Thank you. I’ll go ahead, okay?

631
00:33:52,229 --> 00:33:53,229
Sure.

632
00:34:02,364 --> 00:34:03,656
Is this yours?

633
00:34:03,800 --> 00:34:04,907
I spotted it offstage.

634
00:34:04,908 --> 00:34:06,033
Oh, my goodness!

635
00:34:06,034 --> 00:34:08,829
I thought I’d never see you again!

636
00:34:10,622 --> 00:34:11,706
Thank you!

637
00:34:11,707 --> 00:34:14,208
Thank you so much!

638
00:34:14,209 --> 00:34:15,335
You’re welcome.

639
00:34:15,617 --> 00:34:17,994
You really love your wallet, don’t you?

640
00:34:19,148 --> 00:34:21,448
If it could only talk,
it would probably say

641
00:34:22,068 --> 00:34:24,027
it’s being squeezed to death
by your hugs.

642
00:34:24,052 --> 00:34:24,761
So much.

643
00:34:24,762 --> 00:34:26,262
I was actually planning to walk home.

644
00:34:26,263 --> 00:34:27,983
Because I thought I’d never see this again.

645
00:34:28,490 --> 00:34:29,658
Oh.

646
00:34:29,683 --> 00:34:31,476
So you like going for walks?

647
00:34:31,977 --> 00:34:32,978
A little.

648
00:34:33,228 --> 00:34:36,105
I think I get more than
ten thousand steps a day.

649
00:34:36,106 --> 00:34:39,109
I have to get some walking
since I'm always standing at the mall.

650
00:34:39,735 --> 00:34:40,735
Which mall?

651
00:34:40,861 --> 00:34:42,611
Mega Lux Mall.

652
00:34:42,612 --> 00:34:43,612
Oh.

653
00:34:43,780 --> 00:34:46,115
Did you know that the ten-thousand-step
goal is a marketing myth

654
00:34:46,116 --> 00:34:48,452
created by a pedometer
company in the 1960s?

655
00:34:49,202 --> 00:34:51,955
But it’s still good for you
if you make it a daily goal.

656
00:34:52,831 --> 00:34:55,751
And it’s even better if you combine
it with other types of exercise.

657
00:34:57,294 --> 00:34:58,670
Are you a fitness instructor?

658
00:35:00,464 --> 00:35:01,464
Doctor.

659
00:35:01,590 --> 00:35:03,091
Oh...

660
00:35:08,430 --> 00:35:09,430
By the way, I’m Marvin.

661
00:35:10,390 --> 00:35:11,390
Aira.

662
00:35:13,268 --> 00:35:14,811
It’s a pleasure to meet you, Aira.

663
00:35:18,799 --> 00:35:22,678
You said earlier you’d walk home
if you couldn’t find your wallet.

664
00:35:23,737 --> 00:35:25,784
By any chance,
would you like to ride with me?

665
00:35:26,364 --> 00:35:27,364
Huh?

666
00:35:27,745 --> 00:35:29,038
I can take you home.

667
00:35:29,785 --> 00:35:31,995
Uh...

668
00:35:34,039 --> 00:35:35,456
Um...

669
00:35:35,457 --> 00:35:37,709
Sorry, am I being too forward?

670
00:35:38,001 --> 00:35:39,001
Oh, no.

671
00:35:39,377 --> 00:35:41,629
I actually asked a friend to pick me up.

672
00:35:41,630 --> 00:35:43,298
So I have to wait for him.

673
00:35:45,175 --> 00:35:46,175
Are you sure?

674
00:35:46,468 --> 00:35:47,468
But thank you.

675
00:35:47,691 --> 00:35:49,359
And thanks for returning my wallet.

676
00:35:50,555 --> 00:35:51,681
Okay, uhm.

677
00:35:52,015 --> 00:35:53,725
- I’ll go back to my table.
- Okay, Doc.

678
00:35:54,901 --> 00:35:56,181
- You’re welcome.
- Thank you, Doc.

679
00:35:59,382 --> 00:36:00,967
Thank you, Lord!

680
00:36:01,983 --> 00:36:03,112
Let me check again.

681
00:36:05,932 --> 00:36:06,932
Where is he?

682
00:36:18,166 --> 00:36:19,166
Oh!

683
00:36:20,252 --> 00:36:21,252
Hey, miss.

684
00:36:21,351 --> 00:36:23,437
Weren’t you at the party earlier?

685
00:36:25,040 --> 00:36:27,042
- Uh...
- You were a great host.

686
00:36:27,373 --> 00:36:28,878
Oh, thanks.

687
00:36:30,390 --> 00:36:33,142
Actually, you have a beautiful voice.

688
00:36:33,329 --> 00:36:34,497
It’s captivating.

689
00:36:35,350 --> 00:36:36,852
Oh...

690
00:36:37,936 --> 00:36:40,147
Hey, you’re such a snob!

691
00:36:40,814 --> 00:36:42,274
You’re not even that pretty.

692
00:36:45,652 --> 00:36:46,652
What about you?

693
00:36:47,216 --> 00:36:48,256
You think you’re handsome?

694
00:36:48,976 --> 00:36:49,976
You’re not!

695
00:36:50,458 --> 00:36:51,334
Watch your mouth!

696
00:36:51,438 --> 00:36:52,958
- Stop it!
- Do you want me to kiss you?!

697
00:36:57,455 --> 00:36:59,166
You’re crazy!
Why did you kick me?

698
00:36:59,556 --> 00:37:00,488
You’re right!

699
00:37:00,667 --> 00:37:04,212
You’ll find out how crazy I am
if we cross paths again.

700
00:37:04,838 --> 00:37:05,672
Get over here, hustler!

701
00:37:05,673 --> 00:37:07,193
- Where are you going?!
- Ugh, seriously!

702
00:37:07,218 --> 00:37:08,483
Well, it’s true that I’m a hustler!

703
00:37:08,508 --> 00:37:09,508
And you?

704
00:37:09,593 --> 00:37:11,720
Ugly! Pervert! Mad dog!

705
00:37:12,160 --> 00:37:13,369
- Me? Ugly?
- Yes.

706
00:37:13,628 --> 00:37:14,378
You’re just picky!

707
00:37:14,473 --> 00:37:15,514
You look like a paid escort, anyway.

708
00:37:15,515 --> 00:37:16,183
Cheap!

709
00:37:16,184 --> 00:37:17,474
You only look pretty because I’m drunk.

710
00:37:17,475 --> 00:37:19,602
But once I’m sober,

711
00:37:19,603 --> 00:37:20,855
I wouldn’t touch you.

712
00:37:21,021 --> 00:37:22,146
No one would touch you either.

713
00:37:22,147 --> 00:37:23,315
So, I think it’s a tie.

714
00:37:23,471 --> 00:37:24,917
- What did you say?!
- It’s a tie!

715
00:37:27,110 --> 00:37:28,153
Come here!

716
00:37:28,403 --> 00:37:29,945
- Stand up!
- What?! Let go of me!

717
00:37:30,032 --> 00:37:30,783
- Stand up!
- I said let go!

718
00:37:30,947 --> 00:37:31,823
Come here!

719
00:37:31,824 --> 00:37:34,283
- I’ll teach you a lesson!
- Let go of me!

720
00:37:34,284 --> 00:37:35,577
- Come here!
- Let me go!

721
00:37:52,636 --> 00:37:53,636
Hey!!!

722
00:38:12,823 --> 00:38:13,823
Come here!

723
00:38:14,696 --> 00:38:16,406
Why are you hitting a woman?!

724
00:38:17,301 --> 00:38:18,301
What’s your problem?!

725
00:38:19,243 --> 00:38:20,202
Why are you hitting a woman?!

726
00:38:20,297 --> 00:38:22,214
- Does it hurt?
- Why did you slap me?

727
00:38:22,239 --> 00:38:23,447
- That’s enough!
- Why did you hit her?!

728
00:38:23,472 --> 00:38:24,764
That’s enough.
Just leave him alone!

729
00:38:24,834 --> 00:38:25,834
Enough...

730
00:38:26,695 --> 00:38:27,988
Hey, that’s enough!

731
00:38:28,428 --> 00:38:29,888
- That’s enough.
- You asshole!

732
00:38:35,293 --> 00:38:35,972
What?

733
00:38:36,304 --> 00:38:37,097
Does it hurt more?!

734
00:38:37,098 --> 00:38:38,390
I’ll call the police on you!

735
00:38:38,715 --> 00:38:40,050
I’ll press charges!

736
00:38:40,183 --> 00:38:41,810
My uncle is a prosecutor!

737
00:38:42,313 --> 00:38:43,313
Especially you.

738
00:38:43,413 --> 00:38:45,915
You're nothing but a damn thug!

739
00:38:45,954 --> 00:38:47,497
Nothing but dead weight to society!

740
00:38:47,941 --> 00:38:49,901
What a bunch of morons!
Worthless!

741
00:38:50,297 --> 00:38:51,881
Oh, really? Huh?

742
00:38:51,906 --> 00:38:53,532
Go ahead, try it.

743
00:38:53,697 --> 00:38:55,699
- Aira, Aira.
- I got you on video.

744
00:38:56,024 --> 00:38:57,843
I’ll spread this around
and make you go viral.

745
00:38:57,867 --> 00:39:00,369
Then your family will see
what a pervert you truly are!

746
00:39:00,370 --> 00:39:01,412
Bring it on! Huh?!

747
00:39:01,413 --> 00:39:03,497
- What?! Go ahead!
- Aira, that’s enough. It’s okay.

748
00:39:03,498 --> 00:39:04,874
That’s enough, that’s enough.

749
00:39:05,333 --> 00:39:06,584
Wait, my bag.

750
00:39:07,335 --> 00:39:08,378
Don't test me!

751
00:39:08,883 --> 00:39:09,926
Enough, enough.

752
00:39:10,636 --> 00:39:12,238
- Come on.
- Annoying, what an eyesore!

753
00:39:15,734 --> 00:39:16,902
It’s him again.

754
00:39:23,727 --> 00:39:26,062
So, did you really get
that jerk on video?

755
00:39:27,939 --> 00:39:29,574
No, I was bluffing.

756
00:39:32,084 --> 00:39:33,836
Good thing you think fast, huh?

757
00:39:34,338 --> 00:39:37,300
Otherwise, that jerk
would’ve had us arrested.

758
00:39:40,660 --> 00:39:43,246
It’s been a while since
I saw you kick like that.

759
00:39:44,331 --> 00:39:45,730
How did it feel?

760
00:39:48,752 --> 00:39:49,707
It felt good.

761
00:39:51,862 --> 00:39:52,863
You know what...

762
00:39:54,398 --> 00:39:55,900
I held a mic earlier.

763
00:39:58,887 --> 00:40:00,805
The pay was small, but...

764
00:40:01,973 --> 00:40:03,433
I was so happy.

765
00:40:04,358 --> 00:40:07,191
I’m happy because I got to host again.

766
00:40:07,749 --> 00:40:09,875
And of course, I’m happy for you.

767
00:40:09,900 --> 00:40:13,570
Because at least you got
to show your courage again.

768
00:40:13,610 --> 00:40:14,610
Ouch!

769
00:40:16,321 --> 00:40:17,364
Does it hurt?

770
00:40:18,656 --> 00:40:19,741
What happened?

771
00:40:19,991 --> 00:40:20,950
Is it swollen?

772
00:40:20,950 --> 00:40:21,950
Aira, tell me.

773
00:40:23,870 --> 00:40:26,081
I really should’ve
killed that jerk earlier.

774
00:40:27,540 --> 00:40:28,666
And then you’d go to jail?

775
00:40:32,379 --> 00:40:33,838
I wouldn’t mind going to jail.

776
00:40:35,325 --> 00:40:37,089
They say I’m a failure anyway.

777
00:40:37,967 --> 00:40:39,177
And worthless.

778
00:40:40,387 --> 00:40:41,638
But you, Aira...

779
00:40:42,013 --> 00:40:44,307
Don’t let anyone treat you like that.

780
00:40:44,682 --> 00:40:45,922
You can’t let people abuse you.

781
00:40:47,352 --> 00:40:50,027
Wait, what do you mean
you’re worthless?

782
00:40:54,247 --> 00:40:55,247
Uh...

783
00:40:56,856 --> 00:40:59,620
You heard what that
guy said earlier, right?

784
00:41:01,574 --> 00:41:03,118
That I’m good for nothing.

785
00:41:04,511 --> 00:41:05,620
And...

786
00:41:07,406 --> 00:41:10,183
that I’m an idiot and worthless.

787
00:41:13,044 --> 00:41:14,671
Maybe he’s right.

788
00:41:16,381 --> 00:41:17,632
Hanz.

789
00:41:18,591 --> 00:41:20,927
Yeah, you’re a little stupid,
but you’re not worthless.

790
00:41:21,928 --> 00:41:22,928
You’ll make it big.

791
00:41:23,596 --> 00:41:24,596
I know it.

792
00:41:24,889 --> 00:41:28,143
We’ve known each other
for over 20 years, so trust me.

793
00:41:29,238 --> 00:41:31,078
You’re not a failure.
You still have a future.

794
00:41:31,604 --> 00:41:32,310
Let’s go.

795
00:41:32,335 --> 00:41:34,252
- Wait.
- Let’s go home.

796
00:41:51,583 --> 00:41:53,285
What are you doing?

797
00:41:53,606 --> 00:41:56,192
You’re making me cry.

798
00:41:58,256 --> 00:42:00,008
Are you actually crying?

799
00:42:02,684 --> 00:42:04,061
What do you expect?

800
00:42:05,388 --> 00:42:08,057
I was hungry,
and then you gave me a burger.

801
00:42:08,892 --> 00:42:10,612
And then you gave me
that kind of pep talk.

802
00:42:15,050 --> 00:42:16,566
Come on, hug me.

803
00:42:16,983 --> 00:42:18,442
I’m still holding my burger.

804
00:42:18,443 --> 00:42:19,443
Come on.

805
00:42:20,051 --> 00:42:21,051
Wait.

806
00:42:22,868 --> 00:42:23,911
Is this your butt?

807
00:42:24,657 --> 00:42:26,033
That’s my waist!

808
00:42:26,034 --> 00:42:27,034
Oh!

809
00:42:27,619 --> 00:42:28,828
Aira.

810
00:42:29,829 --> 00:42:31,915
Why do you keep attracting jerks?

811
00:42:33,124 --> 00:42:34,417
Are you a magnet?

812
00:42:35,794 --> 00:42:37,712
Have some pity on yourself because...

813
00:42:39,190 --> 00:42:41,597
you should stay away from people like that.

814
00:42:42,359 --> 00:42:43,694
And Rob...

815
00:42:44,427 --> 00:42:46,554
Can you please stop crying over him?

816
00:42:47,055 --> 00:42:48,639
He’s not worth it.

817
00:42:48,835 --> 00:42:50,535
I don’t like seeing you like this.

818
00:42:52,560 --> 00:42:54,478
- Ouch, ouch!
- Get up already.

819
00:42:54,549 --> 00:42:55,717
That hurts!

820
00:42:57,565 --> 00:42:59,441
Wait, how come you can do that to me?

821
00:42:59,442 --> 00:43:01,495
But when it’s someone else,
you just let them treat you that way.

822
00:43:01,945 --> 00:43:03,530
I kicked that bastard, okay?

823
00:43:04,280 --> 00:43:05,323
Aira.

824
00:43:05,949 --> 00:43:07,242
Just be with me instead.

825
00:43:09,494 --> 00:43:10,472
Choose me.

826
00:43:12,872 --> 00:43:14,332
I promise.

827
00:43:15,083 --> 00:43:16,261
I’ll take care of you.

828
00:43:23,591 --> 00:43:24,592
Are you drunk?

829
00:43:27,428 --> 00:43:30,139
Oh, uh...

830
00:43:30,549 --> 00:43:31,758
No, I said...

831
00:43:33,226 --> 00:43:34,936
I’ll treat you some kikiam.

832
00:43:36,062 --> 00:43:37,146
And beer.

833
00:43:38,027 --> 00:43:39,022
You like that, right?

834
00:43:39,093 --> 00:43:40,595
Uh...

835
00:43:41,335 --> 00:43:42,544
Yeah.

836
00:43:42,829 --> 00:43:43,871
Let’s go.

837
00:44:23,985 --> 00:44:26,820
- Weakling!
- Weakling! Weakling!

838
00:44:26,821 --> 00:44:27,697
What a crybaby!

839
00:44:27,698 --> 00:44:30,199
- Crybaby!
- Hey! What are you doing?

840
00:44:31,242 --> 00:44:32,285
Run!

841
00:44:34,412 --> 00:44:37,707
I can’t work because of you kids!

842
00:44:42,920 --> 00:44:45,214
Why did you even take up Taekwondo?

843
00:44:45,632 --> 00:44:48,216
I told them I’m the prince here.

844
00:44:48,217 --> 00:44:50,970
But they just pushed me.

845
00:44:51,429 --> 00:44:52,555
Here’s how it works.

846
00:44:53,097 --> 00:44:54,556
This is the thumb.

847
00:44:54,557 --> 00:44:55,766
This is you.

848
00:44:55,767 --> 00:44:59,770
Small, a crybaby,
and weaker than the others.

849
00:44:59,771 --> 00:45:02,148
But you’re much cuter.

850
00:45:02,982 --> 00:45:07,654
If you hide it,
no one will know you’re weak.

851
00:45:11,115 --> 00:45:12,324
Open your eyes.

852
00:45:12,325 --> 00:45:14,369
And say you won’t cry anymore.

853
00:45:14,655 --> 00:45:15,907
Next time,

854
00:45:16,329 --> 00:45:17,663
punch them!

855
00:45:17,810 --> 00:45:18,536
Got it?

856
00:45:19,216 --> 00:45:20,832
Even if you’re nice to me,

857
00:45:20,833 --> 00:45:23,753
I still won’t marry you
when I grow up.

858
00:45:25,588 --> 00:45:27,840
I don’t want to marry you either!

859
00:45:29,384 --> 00:45:31,635
Hey, stop crying!

860
00:45:31,636 --> 00:45:33,221
Stop crying.

861
00:45:49,028 --> 00:45:52,406
A few reminders for our dear shoppers.

862
00:45:52,407 --> 00:45:54,866
Outdoor wear is on sale.

863
00:45:54,867 --> 00:45:56,493
If you’re interested,

864
00:45:56,494 --> 00:46:01,123
please visit the event hall on the eighth
floor for great deals and huge discounts.

865
00:46:01,124 --> 00:46:02,541
This is Aira Conti.

866
00:46:02,542 --> 00:46:04,918
And that’s it for this hour’s announcement.

867
00:46:04,919 --> 00:46:06,378
Miss, that’s my friend!

868
00:46:06,379 --> 00:46:08,259
The one who made the
announcement is my friend!

869
00:46:13,344 --> 00:46:14,344
I nailed it!

870
00:46:14,509 --> 00:46:16,345
Why are they such jerks?

871
00:46:17,919 --> 00:46:20,380
They gave it to you,
then took it back?

872
00:46:20,852 --> 00:46:23,396
And they don’t even see
how talented you are!

873
00:46:26,649 --> 00:46:28,109
Cover me.

874
00:46:29,560 --> 00:46:31,604
Hanz, cover me.
